 reference frame (ORB + similarity transform) before the hand-drawn layout and learned scene model are applied."}, {"title": "A crowded scene", "text": "About 50 road users are tracked per analysed frame. Scoring accident risk by 'any close pair' saturated the curve, which is why Part B only considers moving vehicles whose paths actually meet."}, {"title": "Queues follow the signal cycle", "text": "Most stationary vehicles are queued at red or waiting mid-junction for their phase and leave on green - the main source of stopped_vehicle false positives."}, {"title": "Where the events are", "text": "Most real events in our labels are at the two zebra crossings: 21 vehicles passing pedestrians on a crossing (mostly the foreground slip-lane zebra) and 11 people crossing away from the stripes."}], "totals": {"car": 1337, "bus": 69, "person": 2947, "motorcycle": 24, "truck": 65, "bicycle": 8}}